---
import PageLayout from '@/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
const portrait='https://static.wixstatic.com/media/a4f45c_3af2a1300a6d440191dfab00029b44c3~mv2.jpg';
const frontmatter={title:'About',description:'Liviu Bucel — cybersecurity student, technical projects, infrastructure and digital investigations',activeHeaderLink:'About'};
---
<PageLayout {frontmatter}>
  <h1>About me</h1>
  <img src={portrait} width="960" height="960" alt="Portrait of Liviu Bucel" loading="eager" class="float-right mb-5 ml-6 h-40 w-40 rounded-sm object-cover sm:h-56 sm:w-56" />
  <p>I'm Liviu Bucel, a cybersecurity student at <a href="https://www.dmu.ac.uk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">De Montfort University</a> in Leicester, UK. I study how systems fail, how attacks can be detected, and how to investigate incidents using technical evidence.</p>
  <p>My background combines IT support, web infrastructure and hands-on security work. I also build and maintain technical services through <a href="https://www.zebrabyte.ro/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ZebraByte</a>, with a focus on reliable hosting, DNS, TLS and practical security hardening.</p>
  <p>Here I publish what I am building, learning and testing — not just a list of technologies.</p>
  <div class="clear-both"></div>
  <div class="not-prose mt-6 mb-7 flex items-start gap-3 rounded-sm border border-current/20 p-4 text-base">
    <span class="iconify tabler--users-group mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-2xl opacity-70" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <div><p class="font-semibold">OWASP community member</p><p class="mt-1 opacity-80">I am a member of the <a class="clickable underline" href="https://owasp.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Open Worldwide Application Security Project (OWASP)</a> community. Membership is not a certification or endorsement.</p></div>
  </div>


  <h2>What I focus on</h2>
  <p><strong>Application security.</strong> Understanding web vulnerabilities, authentication boundaries, misconfigurations and responsible remediation using tools such as Burp Suite and OWASP guidance.</p>
  <p><strong>Defensive investigation.</strong> Analysing network traffic, interpreting logs and following the evidence through incident response and digital forensics exercises.</p>
  <p><strong>Infrastructure security.</strong> Working with Linux, Windows, DNS, HTTPS/TLS, Cloudflare WAF, rate limiting and practical protection for production websites.</p>

  <h2>Learning and hands-on practice</h2>
  <p>I'm studying BSc (Hons) Cyber Security at De Montfort University (2024–2027 expected). My practical learning includes authorised security assessments, network analysis, incident-response exercises and security-focused technical labs.</p>
  <p>I use Nmap, Wireshark, Burp Suite, Kali Linux and scripting to learn by investigating real system behaviour. Lab exercises are identified as exercises; I do not present them as client engagements or claim unearned qualifications.</p>

  <h2>Projects and technical writing</h2>
  <p>My <a href="/projects/">projects</a> include infrastructure tooling and security-focused applications. Each project page explains what the system does, the technologies involved and the practical problem it addresses. I document research and observations in the <a href="/blog/">blog</a>.</p>

  <h2>Experience and collaboration</h2>
  <p>Before specialising in cybersecurity, I worked with IT support and infrastructure in operational environments. You can see my <a href="/experience/">experience and resume</a> and the <a href="/tools/">tools I actually work with</a>.</p>
  <p>For authorised security assessments, managed Cloudflare configuration or technical collaboration, see <a href="/services/">services</a> or <a href="/contact/">contact me</a>.</p>

  <h2>Find me online</h2>
  <p><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/liviubucel/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a> · <a href="https://github.com/liviubucel" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a> · <a href="https://x.com/liviubucel" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">X</a></p>
</PageLayout>
